  "description": "HAXNUT crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C74 H143 Co3 Gd4 N3 O38,5(H2 O1),C1 H4 O1. From the CIF bond table, Gd2 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd6 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd7 (Gd) has 9 O neighbors; Gd8 (Gd) has 10 O neighbors; Co9 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co12 (Co) has 5 O neighbors; Co14 (Co) has 5 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 10 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.299-5.180 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 98.00-165.65°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [(CoIII)3Gd4(μ3-OH)2(CO3)(O2CtBu)11(teaH)3]·5H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
